    "english_text": "Air means Earth's atmosphere. It is the clear gas we live in and breathe in. It has no color or smell. It has weight. Air creates atmosphere pressure. There is no air in the vacuum and cosmos. Air is a mixture of 78.03% Nitrogen, 20.99% Oxygen, 0.94% Argon, 0.03% Carbon Dioxide, 0.01% Hydrogen, 0.00123% Neon, 0.0004% Helium, 0.00005% Krypton, 0.000006% Xenon. Humans need the oxygen in the air to live. In the human body, the lungs give oxygen to the blood, and give back carbon dioxide to the air. Plants and animals also need air to live: it is very important to everyone.",
    "notes": [
      "Loij = definite article (the)",
      "Lojt = people",
      "'ll = to be"
    ]
  }
}

text_2:
  id: "maliwa_matyna"
  veljano_title: "Lïi maliwa matyna"
  english_title: "A Small Morning"

  veljano: |
    Anna gëauzonwe së a zejsö. Ïn zïmö ŝyi. Ŝï ajmajdwe gëstojwe, abön ŝï musswe gwo zum arbajtö.
    Ŝï ĉajwe baj jesswe së brodwo kèjzot. Sïma kajtïica zejswe en lïi stujlö baj żenojwe ŝwï. 
    «Tü gëluïmwuzë "tajmwe Anna loij kajtïicar" tü ajnpälwu nöd dè arbajtwo».
    Kajtïica ajnretajnwe. Ŝï naet gëojwe s'auz.
    Anna gëpalitove së baj gëbwo lïi bejkwo. Ŝï dürwe nai. Drausp halidwa baj grejwa. 
    Ŝï ahwe baj gwe zum lä busŝtojpö.
    Bïsswemwa ŝï ojwe adiü bussojö. Lojt gwes, on äwlojantwezë baj ŝtajdo gëauzojnwezë. 
    «Djanke luïnwajü tunô» djankwe ŝï.

  english: |
    Anna wakes up at six. The room is quiet. She does not want to get up, but she has to go to work.
    She makes tea and eats bread with cheese. Her cat sits on the chair and watches her.
    "You are lucky," Anna says to the cat. "You do not have to work."
    The cat does not answer. It just closes its eyes.
    Anna puts on her coat and takes her bag. She opens the door. Outside, it is cold and gray. 
    She sighs and walks to the bus stop.
    On the bus, she looks out of the window. People are walking, cars are moving, and the city is waking up.
    "Maybe today will be a good day," she thinks.

